From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: V4L2_DEC_CMD_START clears the last
 buffer dequeued

A drain ends with a CAPTURE buffer flagged LAST, after which videobuf2
answers every DQBUF with EPIPE until the queue's last-buffer state is
cleared. V4L2_DEC_CMD_START resumed the decoder but left that state set,
so a client that drained and started again dequeued nothing more, and
spun on EPIPE.

Clear it on V4L2_DEC_CMD_START, as other stateful decoders do.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 vdec/vdec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff -ruN a/vdec/vdec.c b/vdec/vdec.c
--- a/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -1345,6 +1345,7 @@ vdec_decoder_cmd(struct file *file, void *fh, struct v4l2_decoder_cmd *cmd)
 
 	if (cmd->cmd == V4L2_DEC_CMD_START) {
 		v4l2_m2m_clear_state(sess->m2m_ctx);
+		vb2_clear_last_buffer_dequeued(v4l2_m2m_get_dst_vq(sess->m2m_ctx));
 		sess->should_stop = 0;
 		sess->last_pending = false;
 		sess->draining = false;
-- 
